doc-text-printer-sc-med-advance-directive =
   ⠀          [head=3][color=#5b97bc]Medical Department[/color][/head]
    ══════════════════════════════════════════
   ⠀[color=gray]Instructions for what to do when an individual is killed.[/color]

   ⠀[bold]Patient name:[/bold] [form]
   ⠀[bold]Patient species:[/bold] [form]
   ⠀[bold]Patient gender:[/bold] [form]
   ⠀[bold]Patient pronouns:[/bold] [form]

   ⠀[head=2]Advance Directive[/head]

    The patient states that they trust System Consortium medical and leadership crew to determine her chances of survival and to respect their final decision as to their remains.

   ⠀[head=3]Metempsychosis[/head]

   ⠀[color=#aaaaaa]Select one:[/color]
   ⠀[bullet/][bold][check][/bold] The patient requests that they be put within the metempsychosis machine for revival (commonly known as "cloning"). This directive may be modified after revival.
   ⠀[bullet/][bold][check][/bold] The patient requests that they [bold]not[/bold] be put within the metempsychosis machine for revival (commonly known as "cloning").

   ⠀[head=3]Borging[/head]

   ⠀[color=#aaaaaa]Select one:[/color]
   ⠀[bullet/][bold][check][/bold] In the event of their death, the patient requests that they be put in an MMI and borged, pending the availability of research and materials.
   ⠀[bullet/][bold][check][/bold] In the event of their death, the patient requests that they [bold]not[/bold] be put in an MMI and borged.

   ⠀[head=3]Body replacement[/head]

   ⠀[color=#aaaaaa]Select one:[/color]
   ⠀[bullet/][bold][check][/bold] In the event of a recoverable brain, the patient requests that their brain be implanted in an available body, with the understanding that this body may be that of a reconstituted creature such as a monkey or kobold.
   ⠀[bullet/][bold][check][/bold] In the event of a recoverable brain [bold]and[/bold] torso, the patient requests that their brain be implanted in an available head and attached to their torso with any available limbs.
   ⠀[bullet/][bold][check][/bold] In the event of a recoverable brain [bold]and[/bold] torso, the patient requests that their brain be implanted in an available head and their body cloned in the hopes that the resulting form will be their own.
   ⠀[bullet/][bold][check][/bold] The patient requests that their brain [bold]not[/bold] be implanted in a new head.

   ⠀[head=3]Final alternatives[/head]

    Without the option of recovery or borging, the patient requests that their body be returned to Central Administration for proper cloning and recovery. In the event that their body is destroyed (commonly known as "gibbed"), their brain is to be recovered; in the event that this is not possible, emergency response teams are to perform this task.

   ⠀[head=2]Living will[/head]

    All of the patient's possessions are to be given in trust to the System Consortium and returned to them on revival.

   ⠀[head=2]Medical durable power of attorney[/head]

    The patient bestows medical power of attorney on [bold][form][/bold] who will enforce their wishes and discuss grievances on their behalf.

   ⠀[head=2]Signatures[/head]

   ⠀[color=gray]This document not valid without the stamp of the Chief Medical Officer, Station Administrator, or SysCon/UN representative.[/color]

   ⠀[color=red][bold]X[/bold][/color] [italic][signature][/italic]
   ⠀[head=2]───────────[/head]
   ⠀[bold]Patient signature[/bold]

   ⠀[color=red][bold]X[/bold][/color] [italic][signature][/italic]
   ⠀[head=2]───────────[/head]
   ⠀[bold]Witness signature[/bold]

