doc-text-printer-sc-med-bay-guidelines =
   ⠀          [head=3][color=#5b97bc]Medical Department[/color][/head]
    ══════════════════════════════════════════

   ⠀[head=1]Standards and Expectations[/head]

    These are the standards and expectations to which the medbay and all its personnel are held.

   ⠀[head=2]Cleanliness and sanitation[/head]

   ⠀[bullet/]All medical staff must wear gloves, and all respirating staff must wear a mask (yes, your breath mask works fine) while in the bay. Staff may keep their mask lowered [italic]except[/italic] when performing surgery, where PPE must be worn at all times.
   ⠀[bullet/]There is to be no smoking in the medbay proper, surgery, or chem lab.

   ⠀[head=2]Patient care[/head]

   ⠀[bullet/]Medical personnel are to call out medications being administered before or during administration.
   ⠀[bullet/]Security guidelines, standard operating proceedure, and Syscon policy apply to patients living and dead.

   ⠀[head=3]Surgery[/head]

   ⠀[bullet/]Patients undergoing surgery are to be properly anesthetized (e.g: with nitrous oxide or chloral hydrate) prior to treatment.
   ⠀[bullet/]All surgeries requiring a permit must have such signed and stamped.
   ⠀[bullet/]Surgeries utilizing cybernetics must be approved by the medical department and epistemics as necessary for job function.
   ⠀[bullet/]Surgeries utilizing body parts from corpses of other species specifically for the purpose of attaining benefits of those species are disllowed except in the case of an emergency.
   ⠀[bullet/]Vanity surgeries are not permitted.

   ⠀[head=3]Patient death[/head]

   ⠀[bullet/]All advance directives must be adhered to.
   ⠀[bullet/]All dead patients with recoverable bodies should be revived by means of treatment.
   ⠀[bullet/]All dead patients with unrecoverable bodies should be investigated for any notes on file or jewelry on person containing advance directives in case of their death, which must be obeyed.
   ⠀[bullet/]Without such, the brains of patients with unrecoverable bodies should be placed in an MMI in order to ask their preferences before continuing on to cloning, borging, or brain implantation.

   ⠀[head=2]Conduct[/head]

   ⠀[bullet/]All patients are to be treated with equal respect and the dignity afforded to all sophonts, regardless of their species or status.
   ⠀[bullet/]All patients are to be afforded privacy in treatment and care, and may expect that all information will be kept confidential.
